   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 62 of the laws of 2003, amending the public service\nlaw relating to establishing the New York telecommunications relay service\ncenter, in relation to extending certain provisions of such center",
    "basePrintNo": "S3533",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S3533-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd Part H1 §4, Chap 62 of 2003",
    "lawSection": "Public Services",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S3533\n\nSPONSOR: MAY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 62 of the laws of 2003, amending the public\nservice law relating to establishing the New York telecommunications\nrelay service center, in relation to extending certain provisions of\nsuch center\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis will extend the provisions of law establishing the New York tele-\ncommunications relay service center until June 30, 2027.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection One - Section 1 - Amends section 4 of part H1 of Chapter 62 of\nthe laws of 2003, amending the public service law relating to establish-\ning the New York telecommunications relay service center, as amended by\nChapter 149 of the laws of 2012, Chapter 291 of 2017 and Chapter 58 of\n2020.\n\nSection Two - Establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPublic Service Law section 92-a(2) (a) requires that the New York Tele-\ncommunications Relay Service Center be located in Syracuse, New York.\nThis provision expires on June 1, 2024. This legislation seeks to extend\nthis provision until June 30, 2027.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
